Exercise JSON logging in the telemetry scenario.

Without a job that sets openstack_logging_json, everything this series
adds is code no gate runs.

The telemetry scenario is used because it deploys the OpenStack core
-- Keystone, Glance, Nova and Neutron -- as well as Ceilometer, Aodh
and Gnocchi, so a single job exercises four of the six conversion
batches with services that actually emit oslo.log output. No new job
is added, and a dedicated scenario would have cost six, three
distributions and their upgrades, in both check and gate.

Central logging is deliberately not required for this. The assertions
that matter are that services emit parseable JSON and that Fluentd
reads it, and check-logs.sh already makes both in every job: it treats
Fluentd's "pattern not matched" warnings and error level messages as
critical, so a service whose format the parser cannot read fails the
job. Shipping to OpenSearch would only add the further claim that the
records arrive with the expected field names.

The prometheus-opensearch scenario would have looked like the obvious
home, since it is the only one that enables central logging, but
tests/run.yml disables the OpenStack core services there. Turning the
option on in that scenario sets a flag in a deployment with nothing to
log.

Prompt: Michael asked for phases two and three to be implemented
before anything is pushed, so that the whole story could be reviewed
before it goes public. Checking that story end to end is what found
the empty scenario.

